
P4
========

🔹 Problem Statement
In an identity management system integrated with Active Directory (AD), users may belong to one or more of the following AD groups:

(Admin)

(User)

(Visitor)

The system must generate a three-digit logic code based on the user's membership across these groups:

Group Combination	Logic Code
No group	Null
Only Admin	        100
Only User	        010
Only Visitor        001
Adm + Usr	        110
Adm + Vis	        101
Usr + Vis	        011
Adm + Usr + Vis 	111

Each digit in the code represents membership in one group (ADM, USR, VIS respectively), where:

1 = member

0 = not a member

The objective is to:

Retrieve the user's group memberships from the attribute ds.ldap.memberOf.

Parse the DNs to extract the Common Name (CN) values.

Determine the user's group membership combination across the three known groups.

Based on the combination, assign the correct three-digit logic code.

If the user does not belong to any of the three specified groups, assign the value "Null".

Return the logic code(s) as a SAML attribute.
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
Solution:


#Roles = new java.util.HashSet(), 
#groups = #this.get("ds.opendjds.isMemberOf")!=null?#this.get("ds.opendjds.isMemberOf").getValues():{}, 
#groups.{ #group = #this, #group = new javax.naming.ldap.LdapName(#group), 
#cn = #group.size() == 0 ? "" : #group.getRdn(#group.size() - 1).getValue().toString(), 
#cn.equalsIgnoreCase("User") ? #cn != ("Admin") ? #cn != ("Visitor")? #Roles.add("010") : {} : {} : {},
#cn.equalsIgnoreCase("Visitor") ? #cn != ("Admin") ? #cn != ("User")? #Roles.add("001") : {} : {} : {}, 
#cn.equalsIgnoreCase("Admin") ? #cn.equalsIgnoreCase("User") ? #cn != ("Visitor")? #Roles.add("110") : {} : {} : {}, 
#cn.equalsIgnoreCase("Admin") ? #cn != ("User") ? #cn.equalsIgnoreCase("Visitor")? #Roles.add("101") : {} : {} : {}, 
#cn != ("Admin") ? #cn.equalsIgnoreCase("User") ? #cn.equalsIgnoreCase("Visitor")? #Roles.add("011") : {} : {} : {}, 
#cn.equalsIgnoreCase("Admin") ? #cn.equalsIgnoreCase("User") ? #cn.equalsIgnoreCase("Visitor")? #Roles.add("111") : {} : {} : {},
#cn.equalsIgnoreCase("Admin") ? #cn != ("User") ? #cn != ("Visitor")? #Roles.add("100") : {} : {} : {}},
#Roles.size()==0?#Roles.add("Null") : {},
new org.sourceid.saml20.adapter.attribute.AttributeValue(#Roles)


 
 